Wazuh-agent setup in pfsense

Excellent — wazuh-agent 4.14.6 installed cleanly. Now follow the post-install steps it printed:

1. Copy timezone file:

#sh
#cp /etc/localtime /var/ossec/etc

#2. Set up the config file:

#sh
#cp /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf.sample /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf

#3. Edit ossec.conf to point at your Wazuh manager. Open it and find the <server> block under <client>:

#sh
#cat /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf | grep -A3 "<server>"

#We'll need to set the address to siem machine ip addr - 192.168.30.10. Since multi-line edits are tricky in this shell, use sed for a targeted replace once we see the current placeholder text (paste that grep output).

#4. Set up client keys file:

#sh
#mv /var/ossec/etc/client.keys.sample /var/ossec/etc/client.keys

#5. Enable and start:

#sh
#sysrc wazuh_agent_enable="YES"
#service wazuh-agent start
